{"book": "gate-da", "num": 23, "label": "23", "slug": "23-calculus-differentiability", "title": "Differentiability", "tag": "Calculus & Optimization", "summary": "The derivative of a function $f(x)$ at a point $x = a$ measures the instantaneous rate of change of the function at that point. It is defined as:", "wordCount": 367, "readingTimeMin": 2, "intro": [], "sections": [{"id": "23.1", "title": "Derivatives", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "definition", "name": "Definition", "num": null, "title": "Definition of Derivative", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "The <b>derivative</b> of a function $f(x)$ at a point $x = a$ measures the <b>instantaneous rate of change</b> of the function at that point. It is defined as:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "f'(a) = \\lim_{h \\to 0} \\frac{f(a+h) - f(a)}{h}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "if the limit exists."}, {"t": "p", "x": "Geometrically, the derivative represents the <b>slope of the tangent line</b> to the curve $y = f(x)$ at $x = a$."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Interpretation of Derivative", "blocks": [{"t": "list", "ordered": false, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "If $f'(a) > 0$, the function is increasing at $x = a$."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "If $f'(a) < 0$, the function is decreasing at $x = a$."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "If $f'(a) = 0$, the function may have a local maximum, minimum, or horizontal inflection at $x = a$."}]}]}]}]}, {"id": "23.2", "title": "Examples of Derivatives", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "82", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "{Derivative of a Polynomial}\nFind the derivative of $f(x) = 3x^3 - 5x^2 + 2x - 7$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b> Using the power rule $\\frac{d}{dx}[x^n] = nx^{n-1}$:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "f'(x) = 9x^2 - 10x + 2"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "83", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "{Derivative of a Trigonometric Function}\nFind the derivative of $f(x) = \\sin x + \\cos x$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b> Using standard derivatives $\\frac{d}{dx}\\sin x = \\cos x$ and $\\frac{d}{dx}\\cos x = -\\sin x$:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "f'(x) = \\cos x - \\sin x"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "84", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "{Derivative of an Exponential Function}\nFind the derivative of $f(x) = e^{2x}$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b> Using $\\frac{d}{dx} e^{u} = e^u \\frac{du}{dx}$, here $u = 2x$, $\\frac{du}{dx}=2$:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "f'(x) = 2 e^{2x}"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "85", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "{Derivative of a Rational Function}\nFind the derivative of $f(x) = \\frac{1}{x^2}$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b> Rewrite $f(x) = x^{-2}$, then use the power rule:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "f'(x) = -2 x^{-3} = -\\frac{2}{x^3}"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "86", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "{Derivative Using the Definition}\nFind the derivative of $f(x) = x^2$ at $x = 3$ using the definition:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "f'(a) = \\lim_{h \\to 0} \\frac{f(a+h)-f(a)}{h}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b> Let $a = 3$:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "f'(3) = \\lim_{h \\to 0} \\frac{(3+h)^2 - 9}{h} = \\lim_{h \\to 0} \\frac{9 + 6h + h^2 - 9}{h} = \\lim_{h \\to 0} \\frac{6h + h^2}{h} = \\lim_{h \\to 0} (6 + h) = 6"}]}]}, {"id": "23.3", "title": "Differentiability", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "definition", "name": "Definition", "num": null, "title": "Definition of Differentiability", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "A function $f(x)$ is said to be <b>differentiable at a point $x = a$</b> if its derivative exists at that point:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "f'(a) = \\lim_{h \\to 0} \\frac{f(a+h) - f(a)}{h} \\quad \\text{exists.}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Key Points:</b>"}, {"t": "list", "ordered": false, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "If $f$ is differentiable at $x = a$, then it is <b>continuous</b> at $x = a$."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "The converse is not necessarily true: continuity at $x = a$ does <b>not guarantee differentiability</b>."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Geometrically, differentiability means the function has a <b>well-defined tangent</b> at $x = a$."}]}]}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Geometric Interpretation", "blocks": [{"t": "list", "ordered": false, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "The derivative $f'(a)$ represents the <b>slope of the tangent line</b> at $x = a$."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "If the curve has a sharp corner or cusp at $x = a$, it is <b>not differentiable</b>."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "If the curve has a vertical tangent, $f'(a)$ does not exist, so the function is <b>not differentiable</b> there."}]}]}]}]}, {"id": "23.4", "title": "Checking Differentiability at a Point", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "definition", "name": "Definition", "num": null, "title": "Rule for Checking Differentiability", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "To check if $f(x)$ is differentiable at $x=a$:"}, {"t": "list", "ordered": true, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Check if $f(x)$ is <b>continuous</b> at $x=a$."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Compute the <b>left-hand derivative</b>:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "f'_-(a) = \\lim_{h \\to 0^-} \\frac{f(a+h) - f(a)}{h}"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Compute the <b>right-hand derivative</b>:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "f'_+(a) = \\lim_{h \\to 0^+} \\frac{f(a+h) - f(a)}{h}"}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "If $f'_-(a) = f'_+(a)$ (finite), then $f$ is differentiable at $x=a$. Otherwise, it is not."}]}]}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "87", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Continuity:</b> $|x|$ is continuous at $0$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "Left derivative:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "f'_-(0) = \\lim_{h \\to 0^-} \\frac{|h|}{h} = -1"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Right derivative:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "f'_+(0) = \\lim_{h \\to 0^+} \\frac{|h|}{h} = 1"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Since $f'_-(0) \\neq f'_+(0)$, $f(x)$ is <b>not differentiable</b> at $0$."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "88", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Continuity:</b> $x^2$ is continuous everywhere."}, {"t": "p", "x": "Both derivatives:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "f'(2) = \\lim_{h \\to 0} \\frac{(2+h)^2 - 4}{h} = \\lim_{h \\to 0}(4+h) = 4"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Thus, $f(x)$ is <b>differentiable</b> at $x=2$ with slope $4$."}]}]}, {"id": "23.5", "title": "Visualizing Differentiability", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Curves Illustration", "blocks": [{"t": "fig", "num": null, "figs": [], "srcs": ["/books/gate-da/calc/fig027.png"], "caption": ""}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "89", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Continuity:</b> $\\sqrt{|x|}$ is continuous at $0$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "Left derivative:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "f'_-(0) = \\lim_{h \\to 0^-} \\frac{\\sqrt{-h}}{h} = -\\infty"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Right derivative:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "f'_+(0) = \\lim_{h \\to 0^+} \\frac{\\sqrt{h}}{h} = +\\infty"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Since derivatives diverge, $f(x)$ is <b>not differentiable</b> at $0$."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "90", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "math", "x": "f(x) =\n\\begin{cases}\nx^2, & x \\leq 1 \\\\\n2x-1, & x > 1\n\\end{cases}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Continuity at $x=1$:</b>\nFrom left: $f(1^-)=1$, from right: $f(1^+)=1$. Continuous."}, {"t": "p", "x": "Left derivative:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "f'_-(1) = \\lim_{h \\to 0^-} \\frac{(1+h)^2-1}{h} = 2"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Right derivative:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "f'_+(1) = \\lim_{h \\to 0^+} \\frac{(2(1+h)-1)-1}{h} = 2"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Since $f'_-(1)=f'_+(1)=2$, $f$ is <b>differentiable at $x=1$</b>."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "91", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "{Differentiable Trigonometric Function}\nConsider $f(x) = \\sin x$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b> $f'(x) = \\cos x$, which exists for all $x \\in \\mathbb{R}$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Conclusion:</b> Differentiable everywhere."}]}]}], "sectionCount": 5}